,"categories":[{"description":"Single-player","id":2},{"description":"Steam Achievements","id":22},{"description":"Custom Volume Controls","id":68},{"description":"Mouse Only Option","id":76},{"description":"Playable without Timed Input","id":74},{"description":"Save Anytime","id":79},{"description":"Steam Cloud","id":23},{"description":"Stats","id":15},{"description":"Includes level editor","id":17},{"description":"Family Sharing","id":62}],"content_descriptors":{"ids":[],"notes":null},"demos":[{"appid":3166400,"description":""}],"detailed_description":"<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Astra Ignota</strong> is a minimalist puzzle game set aboard a sentient spaceship adrift between stars.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You must grow <strong>symmetrical galaxies</strong> from their cores outward, fill the entire board, and solve 60 rewarding, handcrafted puzzles, all while uncovering a mysterious sci-fi story told through brief narrative episodes.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The original idea comes from the game <u>Tentai Show</u> (also known as Galaxy), by the Japanese puzzle magazine Nicoli, creators of the <strong>Sudoku</strong>.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The game features multiple grid types, simple gameplay, and multiple tools that get unlocked as the story progresses. And no time pressure. It's about patience, observation, and discovery.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >After a year in <strong>Early Access</strong> gathering feedback and polishing the experience, Astra Ignota is now ready for its full release.</p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >60 pleasant, hand-crafted levels</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Infinite randomly-generated puzzles</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Difficulty ramps up from tutorials to devilish</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A touch of background story, uncovered chapter by chapter</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Beautiful illustrations</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A sooth